==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|colourise||[[:w:British English|Non-Oxford British English]]}}
* {{alt|en|colourize||[[:w:Canadian English|Canadian English]]|[[:w:Oxford Spelling|Oxford British English]]}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|color|ize}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|American spelling}}

# To add color to.
#: {{ux|en|The woman '''colorized''' her hair.}}
# {{lb|en|photography|filmology}} To convert [[black and white]] media to [[color]] by digital post production {{qualifier|as is often done in digital photography and in video special effects}}.
#: {{ux|en|There is a '''colorized''' version of Casablanca.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=August 26, 1988|author=w:Jonathan Rosenbaum|title=Looking for America|work=Chicago Reader|url=https://securesite.chireader.com/cgi-bin/Archive/abridged2.bat?path=1988/880826/SENSES
|passage=What we see are beautiful overlapping NASA satellite photographs of the American mainland, {{...|proceeding sequentially from the east to the west--photographs}}taken in black and white and then luminously '''colorized''' by computer for scientific reasons.}}

